Understanding the Materials Used in Cotton Sanitary Pads

Have you ever wondered what is actually inside a sanitary pad? A sanitary pad may look like a simple product, but it usually contains several layers designed to work together.

The top layer is the part that comes into contact with the skin. Some sanitary pads use cotton or cotton-based materials in this layer. The absorbent core underneath is designed to absorb menstrual fluid, while the bottom layer helps provide leakage protection.

This means that a “cotton sanitary pad” does not necessarily mean that every part of the pad is made from cotton. Different manufacturers may use different combinations of materials.

If you are looking for a cotton sanitary pad, checking the product specifications is therefore important. Look for information about the top sheet, absorbent layer and other product features.

The absorbent core plays an important role in how a pad handles menstrual fluid. Depending on the product, different absorbent materials may be used alongside cotton or other fibres.

The size of the pad also matters. A regular pad may be suitable for some lighter-flow days, while longer or higher-absorbency options may be more appropriate for heavier flow.

Wings are another common feature. They fold around the sides of underwear and can help keep the sanitary pad in place during movement.

Understanding these different components makes it easier to compare products. Instead of choosing a sanitary pad based only on its appearance or name, you can look at the complete design.

If you prefer cotton because of its soft feel, you can specifically look for products that clearly describe their cotton-based material. At the same time, consider absorbency, coverage and fit.

A sanitary pad works as a complete product, with multiple components designed to perform different functions.

Knowing what you are buying can help you make a more informed decision about your period-care products.

